        "repository": "takahirox/gitweave",
        "base": "main",
        "title": "Remove speculative workspace preservation on storage and cleanup failures",
        "body": "Use straightforward workspace cleanup behavior.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nattempt finishes\n  \u2193\nrecord available provenance\n  \u2193\nremove temporary worktree\n  \u2193\nreturn success or failure\n```\n\nDo not preserve temporary worktrees solely because a storage or cleanup failure might be useful for later manual inspection.\n\nDo not maintain special `cleanup_warning` re-recording behavior unless a concrete operational requirement demonstrates that it is necessary.\n\nIf cleanup itself fails, surface that failure directly and keep the behavior simple.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #52."
      }
    },
    "review": {
      "kind": "agent",
      "provider": "codex",
      "workspace_base": 0,
      "instruction": "Follow docs/development-flow.md and docs/review-guidelines.md. Work only in your assigned worktree. Do not delegate or spawn subagents. Do not invoke live agent tests, push, publish, comment/review on GitHub or merge remote state; explicit GitWeave System Actions handle publication. Never redeem usage-limit reset tickets, buy allowance, or switch models/providers to bypass limits. Stop and return blocked if an actual permission/capability limitation prevents completion; do not invent an unsupported workaround or weaken requirements. Ordinary code/test defects are fixable findings, not capability blockers. Keep project material in English. Use deterministic tests and preserve existing behavior outside the issue's explicit change. Do not alter other worktrees or the original checkout.\n\nReview the complete current PR artifact against Issue #52 and repository guidelines. Inspect the full diff from original main 9adf00c3a324f62306c3eba90335fccbf3424569, not just the last checkpoint. The upstream publish result provides its URL; review the artifact locally and read the PR CI results. Check missing and excess scope, actual behavior, failure/edge cases, compatibility and test coverage. The issue intentionally changes a default, so verify the new default and retained explicit behavior. Relevant scope guidance:\nImplement the supplied issue and accepted clarification only. Keep the change minimal, preserve unrelated existing behavior, and update focused deterministic tests and current documentation. Do not implement other open Issues in this PR. This issue intentionally simplifies existing behavior; do not recreate the removed policy as a new abstraction.\nDo not modify project files. Run relevant deterministic checks. Additionally use read-only gh pr checks on the upstream published PR URL and wait for its CI checks to complete before approval (gh pr checks URL --watch --interval 10). Reading GitHub checks/logs is explicitly allowed despite the no-remote-mutation rule. Inspect failed-job logs and return changes_requested for fixable test/code failures; blocked for actual capability/permission/allowance problems. Do not rerun CI, bypass checks or approve failed/cancelled checks without resolving the cause. Return approved only with no actionable findings and passing checks; otherwise changes_requested with concrete file/behavior findings, or blocked for a capability limitation.",
